# VISTA design standards

For **any UI, UX, or visual design work** in this project, treat **VISTA** as the single source of truth—not ad-hoc styles or generic component libraries.

## Canonical docs (Storybook)

- **Base:** https://marketplace.wdprapps.disney.com/storybook/
- **Changelog / release notes:** https://marketplace.wdprapps.disney.com/storybook/?path=/docs/changelog--docs
- **Product:** RA Web Components — **Vista Library** (DX Marketplace)

## What to follow from Storybook

- **Architecture:** Configure Web Components, Angular, or React per project stack
- **Theme:** Typography (modes, size ramps), Colors, Motion tokens, Theme Colors
- **Components:** Use documented `wdpr-*` patterns and props; prefer library components over one-offs
- **Toolbar context:** Global theme (e.g. Vista — Parks Now), typography **Mode** (`data-mode` tiers), responsive typography when Mode is Auto

## Agent access

- Internal `wdprapps.disney.com` URLs often **fail** via server-side fetch; use the **Cursor browser** to open Storybook on the user’s network/VPN when verifying specs, changelog entries, or component APIs.

## Design work checklist

1. Check Storybook for the relevant component or theme doc before implementing.
2. Match tokens (typography, color, motion)—do not invent parallel naming.
3. Note library version from **Changelog** when behavior or props may have changed recently.
